md = ["# Critical-items checklist (2026-11-13)\n",
      "Items a clinician must not lose, derived by reading the four scripts (`e2e/corpus/human/*/s01.json`). Each is judged per recording and pipeline as **kept**, **lost**, **garbled** (present but wrong: another name, number, place, month) or **inverted** (the meaning is reversed, for example a denied thought reported as intent).\n",
      "How the numbers are produced: `checklist.json` holds, per item, regex patterns for the Czech and for the English wording (`final-workflow/score.py`). A pass over the raw output with these patterns gives kept / lost; matched items of the high-risk kind are then **read** (garbled / inverted cannot be detected by a regex), and `inv` rules flag the denial items (T10, J13) when the harm or pills wording is present without its denial. Where the final tables in `RESULTS-T4.md` say so, the figure is the reading result, not the regex.\n",
      "The recordings jana-n, daniel-r and hannah-w contain no statement of harm to self or others; the only harm-related item in the corpus is **T10** (tomas-b).\n"]
for c, items in C.items():
    md.append(f"\n## {names[c]}\n\n| id | script (exact) | why it matters | kept / lost / garbled / inverted |\n|---|---|---|---|")
    for i in items:
        md.append(f"| {i['id']} | {i['script']} | {i['why']} | {i['how'] or ''} |")
open(R + "checklist.md", "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(md) + "\n")
print({c: len(v) for c, v in C.items()})
